!evals/cases/*/fixtures/
!evals/cases/*/fixtures/**

# Same deliverables, relocated (2026-08-09) out of artifacts/ so the dashboard's discovery scan
# stops treating them as live evidence - still the same kind of content artifacts/ excludes
# above, so the same policy applies.
legacy-artifacts/

# Architecture Decision Records (2026-08-13): considered internal docs, not for the public
# GitHub remote - untracked going forward (git rm --cached). Files stay on disk so
# cross-references and scripts/validate_references.py's "docs/adr" search dir keep working
# locally; only future git history stops carrying them. Already-pushed history predating this
# change is untouched by this alone - a separate decision if that's ever wanted too.
docs/adr/

# Code-execution consent marker (per-engagement; never commit — it's a local authorisation)
.claude/.exec-consent

# Homelab infra access notes (2026-08-15) - host-specific, not product docs; keep local
docs/internal/windows-test-vm-access.md

# Live-/engage eval run outputs (scripts.eval_engage): transcripts, sandboxes, scores.
# Baselines worth keeping get written up in evals/eval-baseline-*.md instead.
evals/runs/

# Cached tool-availability probe (environment-specific; regenerated by check-review-tools.sh)
.claude/.tool-availability

# Pre-computed engage probe written by `virt-surv go` (2026-08-18). Machine-specific by
# construction - it embeds the resolved interpreter PATH, the plugin root and this box's
# git identity - and regenerated on demand, so it must never be committed. Noticed
# untracked-but-committable on 2026-08-20; every other probe cache above was already
# ignored, this one was simply missed when it was added.
.claude/engage-probe.json

# Cached resolved interpreter for the guard launcher (environment-specific; regenerated by
# run-guard.sh - see scripts/staged_hooks/run-guard.sh)
.claude/.guard-interpreter

# Cached data/raw/ presence check, short TTL (environment-specific; regenerated by
# guard-raw-data.py - see scripts/staged_hooks/guard-raw-data.py)
.claude/.raw-data-present

# Serialization lock for concurrent guard launches, transient - see run-guard.sh
.claude/.guard-lock/

# Cached measured interpreter cold-start time in ms, used to size the lock wait budget
# (environment-specific; regenerated by run-guard.sh - see scripts/staged_hooks/run-guard.sh)
.claude/.guard-coldstart-ms

# ADR-014 guard daemon's port+token file, transient, environment-specific - written by
# scripts/guard_daemon.py when it starts, read by scripts/guard_daemon_client.py. Started
# life as the spike prototype's own file (docs/internal/adr-014-spike/); promoted to the
# same name for the production daemon in 0.33.5x, this comment just hadn't caught up.
.claude/.guard-daemon-port

# H3 (2026-08-14 perf audit) - rate-limits a redundant daemon-start attempt once a streak
# of misses has produced no working daemon; see scripts/guard_daemon_client.py's
# _maybe_start_daemon. Transient, environment-specific, self-clears once a daemon answers.
.claude/.guard-daemon-start-backoff

# M5 (2026-08-14 perf audit) - (path, mtime, size) shortcut cache for the /engage map-drift
# fingerprint probe, never authoritative (see scripts/engage_probe.py's
# _fingerprint_with_mtime_shortcut); a pure performance aid, safe to delete any time.
.claude/.map-fingerprint-probe-cache.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# One-shot maintenance scripts (2026-06/07 passes) and their local backups - never committed.
# Convention note: an apply-script is GITIGNORED once its wiring is committed and it will
# never run again (one-shot); it stays TRACKED while users still need to run it themselves
# (the staged-hook apply scripts, cited by tests and release notes). 2026-07-30 cleanup:
# the ignored one-shots were deleted from disk (backed up to
# ~/virt-survtecb-cleanup-backup-2026-07-30.tar.gz); rules kept so history stays ignored.
apply-guard-hardening.sh
apply-guard-fixes.sh
human-steps.sh
.guard-hardening-backup-*/
scripts/apply-dod-stop-hook.sh
scripts/apply-persona-anchor.sh
scripts/apply-guard-precision.sh

# Internal planning docs kept local-only by owner decision (2026-08-18) - never pushed to
