# Local test containers (2026-08-25, owner: "should not be put on git").
# Host-specific infra: it names this machine's paths and mounts this machine's credentials.
# Deliberately not shipped - a container definition that assumes one developer's box is worse
# than none, because it looks portable and is not.
docker/

# Rendered demo output (2026-08-29): every file here is generated from its .md sibling by
# scripts/render_html.py, so tracking it version-controls build output. The .md is the
# source and is tracked; regenerate with `python -m scripts.render_html <file>.md`.
# NOT applied to evals/cases/**: those .html files are FIXTURES - they define the workspace
# a case starts from, so removing them would change what the eval sees.
docs/demos/**/*.html

# DLP blocked terms - NEITHER file is ever committed.
#
# .dlp-keywords.local  the terms themselves, plaintext.
# .dlp-blocklist       SHA-256 digests of those terms.
#
# The digest file was going to be committed so a fresh clone inherited the protection.
# It is not, because a digest of a short unsalted word is a confirmable fingerprint: a
# stranger who merely GUESSES a blocked term can prove the guess with one sha256 call.
# In a public repo that is an oracle for exactly the words we refuse to publish. The
# scanner (scripts/dlp_guard.py) carries no terms and no digests, so it commits freely;
# the list reaches CI through the DLP_BLOCKLIST repo secret instead.
.dlp-keywords.local
.dlp-blocklist
